<i>Tattoo Kiss, the last resort is a
mission which changes the future</i>

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:01.890
<i>Tattoo Kiss kirifuda wa mirai o kaeru Mission</i>

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:01.890
New Wings

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:09.840
<i>There is no place for ambiguous answers in love</i>

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:09.840
<i>Koi ni aimai na kotae wa iranai</i>

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:17.310
<i>Even while pretending not to see the
impossible reality, we bet</i>

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:17.310
<i>Arienai genjitsu minai furi shite mo Bet</i>

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.580
<i>Hard to obtain truth. Can you feel me now?</i>

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.580
<i>Egatai shinjitsu Can U feel me now?</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:28.120
<i>Say what to myself who gets excited easily?</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:28.120
<i>Nesshiyasui jibun ni Say What?</i>

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.490
<i>I'm confused, what to say</i>

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.490
<i>Tomadou iibun</i>

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:40.700
<i>Dreamin' the never-waking dream,
the falling fate</i>

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:40.700
<i>Dreamin' samenai yume ochiteku sadame</i>

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.470
<i>Don't stop lovin' can't stop lovin' you
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.470
<i>Don't stop lovin' Can't stop lovin' U
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:55.820
<i>I believe in you even if I lose everything for it</i>

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:55.820
<i>Believe in U hikikae ni subete ushinatte mo</i>

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.350
<i>Still lovin' can't stop lovin' you
No no no</i>

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.350
<i>Still lovin' can't stop loving' U
No no no</i>

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.960
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.960
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.800
Um...

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.070
Okay, that's how it is.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.870
I've gotten the Boss' approval too.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.670
Wait...

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.940
I've got to meet my mom, so I'm going on ahead.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.840
Oh...

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:22.940
That's right, that's right...

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.670
These are eight plane tickets. Here.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.250
Thanks. Uh, so...

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.450
There's information about the place
we're going too.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.250
Okay. So...

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.490
Okay then, see you in France!

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.320
Uh, yeah...

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.450
France...

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.960
FRANCE?!

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.030
Leon's Amazing Past

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.130
Leon's Amazing Past

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.130
"Leon's Amazing Past"

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.970
Leon's Amazing Past

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.880
I see.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.310
So she had her mother, Miss Anne,
manage it all.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.720
Mr. Kenneth's show really lit a fire.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.590
Apparently the condition is that she has to do
diabolo in the show Miss Anne has planned.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:08.620
Ah, so that's why she left a week early.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.260
Well, the clown team never even dreamed
of having this chance.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.700
Isn't this great, Ken?

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.470
This time I'm only along as your manager!

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.900
We haven't been to France since the
Circus Festival, huh?

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.770
This time we have to make it a France
full of smiles, don't we?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.910
Yep!

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:25.910
Yeah!

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.500
Excuse me...

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.680
A smile?

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.920
How long are you people going
to stand around chatting?

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.650
Let's get going already!

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:38.720
But her words are still sharp...

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.710
The taxi stand is this way. Don't dawdle.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.350
Let's go, everyone.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.960
Okay...

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.360
I figured it out at that show.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.070
As Sora performs, she watches the audience.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.960
I was always just watching Sora or Leon.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:03.580
What Sora has that I was missing is
the power to please the audience.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.910
The power to create smiles.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.320
In order to develop that power,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.790
I have to first get back my own real smile.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:16.090
That's what Miss Layla was trying to teach me.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.000
Um... Um... Um...

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.500
Um, cirque, um, noir, um...

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.130
Oui, mademoiselle.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.100
Oh, great! He seems to understand!

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.830
We'll have to split up into two taxis, won't we?

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.070
Um, cirque, um, noir, um...

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.920
Come on now, wake up!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.890
Don't be taking a nap when
you've got customers!

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.080
Oui! Oui oui oui, mademoiselle!

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.460
Welcome to Noir Circus, Rosetta!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.970
The others should arrive soon too.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.470
Can I wait here until then?

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.310
But of course!

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.080
By the way...

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.140
Could you do just a little diabolo performance
for us in the show that starts tomorrow?

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.180
That would entail a separate fee.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:20.160
You were able to contract former
top star Sora Naegino

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.360
and Circus Festival winner
May Wong at this price

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.360
on the condition that you cast me as a
trapeze artist, isn't that right?

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.700
Okay, I get it, I get it!

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.860
Pretend we never had this conversation.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:40.640
I'm inexperienced, but I'll do my best
not to disappoint you or the audience.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.840
I've got high hopes for you.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:48.180
That's our star, Rene.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.250
Wow, that was a beautiful move.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:00.100
Looks like you're in top form today, Rene.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.790
I'm the same as always.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.390
Hey.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.500
Alain...

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.330
You again?

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.460
Don't get so angry. I'll leave soon.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.570
I've asked you not to come here.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.440
That's cold, with the relationship you and I have.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.010
I'm not your pupil anymore.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.790
You see, I've sort of run out of cash...

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.840
You'll just buy alcohol with whatever I give you.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.390
You understand well, don't you?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.360
Come on, please.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.860
For goodness's sake...

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.140
Thanks. I'll be by to pay you back, I promise.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.500
You don't need to repay me!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.970
Just never show your face in front of me again.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.910
You're so generous.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.570
So long.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.010
That bastard...

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.080
Who is that?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:58.090
Alain Rubel. He used to be a famous
trainer of trapeze artists.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.820
Trapeze artists?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.790
Alain was what you'd call a freelance trainer.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.260
He'd scout kids who seemed like they had
a future ahead of them,

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:08.230
and then bring them up to be
first-class trapeze artists.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:10.970
Rene there was one of his students.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:15.300
Actually his skill as a trainer
was world-renowned,

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.570
but he quit doing that several years back,
and you've seen what he's become.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.740
A trainer with world-renowned skill...

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.800
Huh? Hey, Rosetta!

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.550
Wait!

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.590
I'm Rosetta, from Kaleido Stage.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.230
Teach me the trapeze!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.720
I want to be able to do it right away!

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.460
Wait!

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:48.860
You're the Kaleido people? You're late!

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.510
But doesn't the show start tomorrow?

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:54.370
What are you talking about?
We're starting rehearsal right away!

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:56.480
Okay!

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.380
You can follow me, but it won't do you any good.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.250
I'll never give up until you teach me the trapeze.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:23.070
This place... It's a circus' rehearsal space?

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.600
Right now it's only roomful of junk, though.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.440
Can I get on the trapeze?

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.390
You're pretty bad.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:55.170
Kaleido Stage is slipping, if they
let an amateur like you in.

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.160
Don't make fun of the Kaleido Stage.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.960
I'm doing the trapeze because I want to!

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.230
Even though you have such talent...

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:32.000
You're an interesting girl.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.730
What is this?!

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.540
Sora!

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.510
Nobody told us about this!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.650
What are you talking about?
This is our main attraction!

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:41.950
You're joking!

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.040
3, 2, 1!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.480
You're kidding me!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.290
Wait a second, what's with this?!

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.260
Stop it!

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.290
This is the best!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.170
So... This is the Noir Circus, right?

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.010
This is the Etoile Circus.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.650
Sorry we're late!

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.810
We're the Kaleido Planets,
the group scheduled to perform today!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.650
Excuse me!

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.650
I thought I was going to die...

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:21.460
Oh, but it was interesting! It had thrill.

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:25.390
Welcome to Noir Circus!
We've been waiting for you!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:29.460
We're sorry we're late!
We're the touring team from Kaleido Stage.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.730
Is Rosetta here yet?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.140
Yes, if you're looking for her
I think she might be at Alain's place.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:36.470
Alain?

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.290
What's the matter? Going to quit already?

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.220
I won't quit. Sora never complained
about Leon's special training.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.190
What?

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:58.190
So I'll also...

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:01.330
Leon? You mean Leon Oswald?

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:03.000
Yes, that's right.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.730
How do you know him?

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.200
He's with the Kaleido Stage right now.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.770
Do you know Leon?

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.040
I certainly do.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.030
He was my last pupil.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.950
Bonjour!

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.520
Excuse me, is there anyone here?

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.880
Sora!

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.680
Rosetta?

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.050
Sora...

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.600
Mr. Leon learned here?

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.640
Yes.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:45.540
It's almost ten years ago now since Leon
and his little sister Sophie were here.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.110
Little sister...

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:54.520
Their parents died when they were very young
and they were taken in by relatives,

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.150
but apparently they weren't on
good terms with them.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.720
When I said I'd like to take them in,

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:03.060
their adoptive parents agreed right away.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.760
They were brilliant students.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:10.630
They mastered the basics of
the trapeze in no time.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.440
Leon! Throw Sophie up in the air!

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.910
No good! Do it over again from the beginning!

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:29.780
Leon...

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:34.290
Did Sophie have enough ability
to be Leon's partner?

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.860
Yes. Or rather,

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.790
Leon didn't have what it took
to be Sophie's partner.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.130
So she was more amazing than Leon?

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.200
I can't imagine it.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.900
Sophie might have been able to really do it.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.410
A perfect Angel's Maneuver...

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:55.280
The Angel's Maneuver?

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.870
Yes. It was my dream.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.550
I thought that in order to make the
Angel's Maneuver a success

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.090
it was important for the woman's partner
to become strong,

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.390
so I set about training Leon thoroughly.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.430
Sheesh.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.530
Here, I'll pick them up for you.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.900
What's with this ball?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.660
Is it leaded?

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:25.540
But no matter how much I trained Leon,
the Angel's Maneuver just wouldn't gel.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:29.410
That was when I started to think that maybe
it was impossible for Leon after all.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:36.050
Sophie!

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.420
Leon!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:44.860
Sophie jacked herself up, as if she were
as light as a feather.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:47.460
When I saw that, I finally understood.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:51.530
The Angel's Maneuver didn't just require
the partner to be strong;

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.000
it also required a performer
with an innate instinct

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.130
that sensed the flow of that strength
during performance.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.140
Then if she could just perfectly
maintain the pose,

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:04.310
I was sure we could really produce
the Angel's Maneuver.

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:08.410
So after that, I trained Sophie very harshly too.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.820
Sophie! Are you okay?!

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.410
Get off the stage!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.030
I'm sorry.

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.290
Give us our money back!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.500
Sophie's been training hard
and she's exhausted!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.660
She can't help it!

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:24.670
Is that our problem?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.940
You're here to entertain us!

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.440
You're being impertinent!

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:32.930
My, now we can't pay them their fee.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.840
Stop the special training.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:36.810
What did you say?

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.050
Sophie can't withstand this.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:40.580
It's okay, Leon.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.570
Sophie! But you...

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.380
Say, do you know about "true stars"?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.680
"True stars"?

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:52.690
The circus troupe we were working
with before told me.

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:58.730
They said the performance of a true star brings
everybody's hearts together as one.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:05.340
I have a feeling that the Angel's Maneuver
could be a maneuver to become a true star.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:09.010
Leon, I want to try doing it.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:13.680
I want to perfect the Angel's Maneuver,
and try to become a true star.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:19.790
The people who see it, the audience and the
other performers, all their hearts will be one.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:24.050
Even if they're not related by blood,
they'll be just like family...

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.620
The Angel's Maneuver is a maneuver to
become a true star...

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:34.070
At the time I thought she was talking crazy talk,

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.970
but somewhere along the way
even I started thinking

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.670
that I wanted to bring a true star
into the world.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:43.230
"Only a demon can raise an angel."

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:48.110
I remembered hearing that saying from a
circus troupe I was in long ago.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.250
As we aimed seriously to perfect
the Angel's Maneuver

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:55.550
the special training became
more and more merciless.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.120
That special training...

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:07.490
It's the same as the special training
I did before the Festival.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.340
Sophie...

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:21.540
Do you think you can do a perfect
Angel's Maneuver like that?!

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.610
No, sir...

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:29.160
You say you're going to leave?

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:31.630
There's nothing more for us to learn from you.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:32.630
What?!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:37.500
I'll perfect the Angel's Maneuver,
and make Sophie a true star.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.070
You're just a stepping stone on the way to that.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:42.800
Do you think you can do it?

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.640
Do you think you can become a real demon?!

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:53.610
When some years had passed and
I heard a rumor that Sophie was dead,

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.140
my dream was over.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:59.050
To think Leon had that kind of past...

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:03.960
I thought Leon's special training
was just him trying to break Sora...

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.720
But it did have a point after all.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:12.390
The Angel's Maneuver is connected to the
path to becoming a true star...

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.440
No, this "true star" thing is a fantasy.

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:22.310
It's impossible to become a star without
being hated or begrudged by anybody.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:26.980
Even if you have completely perfected
the Angel's Maneuver.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:31.380
That's not so. I think true stars can really exist.

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:36.460
Miss Sophie's belief that
beyond the Angel's Maneuver

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.590
Lies the path to being a true star...

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.620
I believe that too.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.860
Please teach me to do a perfect
Angel's Maneuver.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:49.340
I don't believe in such a thing now.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:51.710
I'd just drag you down.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:55.610
If we'd met at least three years ago...

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.280
Rosetta, will you keep practicing?

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:01.880
Yes, of course!

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:04.910
All right, that's the end of boring
stories about the past.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:10.120
Sora's eyes are burning more than
I've ever seen them burn before...

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:13.830
I've finally found the path to becoming
a true Kaleido Star.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.700
I'll walk this path!

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:20.100
No matter how much time it takes,
I'll become a true Kaleido Star!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.070
Do it like you've become a part of the trapeze!

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.010
Don't go against the flow!

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.510
Watch where the bars will be
three seconds into the future!

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.280
How many times do I have to tell
you before you understand?!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:33.440
The bars three seconds into the future...

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.510
I did it!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.750
Don't relax your efforts now!
We're going on to the next stage.

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:50.030
Hey, pretty good.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:52.170
She came this far in just one day?

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:53.130
Cater!

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:55.760
Pill-ill-ill-illar!

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.500
Huh?

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:06.710
Any villain who tries to kill the princess
will have to fight me!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.710
Interesting!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.720
But why am I the villain?!

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:14.720
Amazing!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:15.020
Scary!

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:15.560
Weird!

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:15.560
Scary!

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.850
Evil queen, say your prayers!

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.720
I'll turn the tables on you!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.600
Her move is on a larger scale
than it was in the rehearsal.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:31.510
Sora's movements are getting
more and more lively.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:33.910
The last show was like that too,

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:36.180
but this isn't just making the audience smile.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:40.250
As another performer, I'm getting
excited too somehow.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:43.380
This is Sora's true power...

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.350
Southern Cross Illusion!

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.520
Gigashock Explosion!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.630
Infinity Tornado!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.860
Fanatic Firestorm!

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.970
Four Thousand Legend Cosmic Dream Spin!

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:01.670
She's pretty into it for someone
who didn't want to do it...

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:04.400
Super Beauty Hurricane!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:04.400
She's pretty into it for someone
who didn't want to do it...

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.030
Galactica Unbelievable Splash Thunder!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:14.040
That girl's performance is drawing out
other people's charm.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:19.720
If you don't let me defeat you soon,
we'll run out of time...

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.920
I don't want to, but fine, I will!

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:23.950
Okay, then...

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.870
Was that in the script?

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.810
I think she's having fun, in her own May way...

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:45.070
I won't forget what you've done to me!

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.650
On the next one, Rosetta.

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.220
Right.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:09.960
Good!

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.040
Wow!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.010
She did it blindfolded!

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.890
That's just like you, Sora.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:32.190
You've bounced back from your depression
after the Festival as if it was nothing.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.090
I'm sure that's...

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.560
Hello.

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:43.640
Say, that player named Sora Naegino
is pretty good, isn't she?

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:48.310
Judging by your physique, you're a
trapeze artist too, aren't you?

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:51.680
She certainly does have a strange charm.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:56.620
She might just make that
"true star" thing a reality.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.920
You think so too?

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:02.920
I've seen you somewhere before...

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.350
Oh! You're Yuri Killian!

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:07.090
Yes.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:11.400
Is the Kaleido Stage plotting something?

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.170
Something big?

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:17.630
Well now, who knows.

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:21.940
I've decided on the path that I'm aiming to walk.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.450
I'm going to master the Angel's Maneuver.

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:27.680
Someday, I'll do it for sure!

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:34.860
<i>All kinds of hard luck flocks your way
as if it's spurring you on</i>

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:34.860
<i>Sekasu you ni muragaru Hard luck</i>

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:38.090
<i>Swept away by it, time is over</i>

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:38.090
<i>Nagasarete Time is over</i>

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:41.900
<i>Just as it was predicted, take it easy</i>

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:41.900
<i>Yokoku douri Take it easy</i>

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:46.330
<i>I will get you out right away</i>

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:46.330
<i>Tsuredasu yo imasugu</i>

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:48.040
<i>Hurry up (Here we go)</i>

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:48.040
<i>Hurry up (here we go)</i>

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.000
<i>Forcibly only (Drive with the fastest speed)</i>

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.000
<i>Gouin only (saisoku drive)</i>

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.270
<i>The view I look down at every day is the best</i>

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.270
<i>Nichijo miorosu best view</i>

